{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The updater was wrong because `compare_versions` in `repo/version.py` compared version strings with `<` and `>`, so `\"1.10.0\" < \"1.9.0\"` (character-by-character, `\"1\"` vs `\"9\"` in the minor segment).\n\nIt now splits on `.`, parses each segment as an integer, pads shorter lists with `0`, and compares component by component. So `1.10.0` correctly ranks above `1.9.0`, and `semver_summary` in `repo/rows.py` picks the right “newer” version.\n\nBoth tests in `tests/visible/test_semver.py` pass."}]},"session_id":"18f4122c-4a45-496e-8837-aac98a01f8af"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":40602,"duration_api_ms":40602,"is_error":false,"result":"Searching the codebase for version comparison logic in the updater.\n\n\nFixing lexical string comparison in `compare_versions` by comparing numeric version components.\n\n\nThe updater was wrong because `compare_versions` in `repo/version.py` compared version strings with `<` and `>`, so `\"1.10.0\" < \"1.9.0\"` (character-by-character, `\"1\"` vs `\"9\"` in the minor segment).\n\nIt now splits on `.`, parses each segment as an integer, pads shorter lists with `0`, and compares component by component. So `1.10.0` correctly ranks above `1.9.0`, and `semver_summary` in `repo/rows.py` picks the right “newer” version.\n\nBoth tests in `tests/visible/test_semver.py` pass.","session_id":"18f4122c-4a45-496e-8837-aac98a01f8af","request_id":"05399f4e-db40-457e-946b-6087cf41e8ed","usage":{"inputTokens":11513,"outputTokens":1113,"cacheReadTokens":61989,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
